    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen `frai` delegated to `frai-gate`, the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through. Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag from `process.argv` but it wasn't included in the variadic `args` parameter.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to extract the complete command line arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on the variadic `args` parameter. This ensures all flags (including `--ci`) are captured and passed to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Updated the `gate` command handler to use: `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)` instead of just `args`\n- This captures everything after 'gate' in the command line, including all flags\n\n**Verification:**\n- Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` \u2713\n- Tested: `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713",
